decision: changes-requested

The four prior findings are fixed in their reported scenarios. Three high-severity blockers remain:

- **N24:** Gitlinks nested inside modules bypass the symlink scan.
- **N25:** Nested-module changes can leave enclosing-module checks carried.
- **N26:** Case-folding ancestors can evade the filesystem alias guard.

`go test ./...`, build, vet, targeted regressions, artifact-check, and repository-wide strict validation passed. The separate module-only validator failed on read-only scratch creation; its checks passed in the full validator. Persisting assessments were skipped because scratch creation was blocked. New findings are based on source traces and in-memory predicate probes, not newly executed fixtures.

Applied the Go backend, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. No repository changes or attestation were written.

